  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+3\\,=\\,4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+3\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+4x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+0x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}-8x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}+x-2}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,9x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $4{x}^{2}+4x-1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-9x+5.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+3}{\\,{x}^{2}-x+2\\,}=\\,4{x}^{2}+4x-1\\,+\\frac{\\,(-9x+5)\\,}{\\,{x}^{2}-x+2\\,}.\n$$",
